| **3** | **Safety & Compliance Regulations**   | Critical for crew; covers STCW updates, ISM Code, SOLAS, and risk management.                           | Officers, superintendents, ship managers.    | Case studies, regulatory changes, safety drills (fire, abandon ship), OSH certification prep.       |
| **4** | **Maritime Technology & Automation** | Future-proofing; covers AI in shipping, digital charts (ECDIS), remote operations, and cybersecurity.   | Tech-savvy students, engineers.              | Interviews with tech firms, comparisons (traditional vs. digital navigation), certs like **IAMI**.   |
| **5** | **Environmental Impact & Sustainability** | Growing focus; ESG (Environmental, Social, Governance) in shipping, green shipping certs (e.g., **IMO 2020**). | Eco-conscious students, sustainability officers. | Carbon footprint calculators, alternative fuels (LNG, biofuels), regulatory changes (e.g., **IMO 2030**). |
| **6** | **Maritime Law & Legal Issues**      | Practical for officers; covers contracts, liability, maritime courts, and labor laws.                   | Legal officers, superintendents.           | Sample contracts, case law summaries, labor rights (e.g., **MSC Convention**), insurance basics.    |
| **7** | **Navigation & Pilotage**             | Core skill; covers AIS, radar, ECDIS, and pilotage procedures.                                         | Deck officers, pilots.                     | Hands-on tutorials, real-world scenarios (e.g., **Pilotage Rules**), collision avoidance drills.     |
| **8** | **Engineering & Machinery Systems**  | High demand; covers diesel engines, propulsion, HVAC, and electrical systems.                          | Engineers, ETOW candidates.                 | Troubleshooting guides, maintenance schedules, certs like **ETOW (Engineer’s Watch Officer)**.      |
| **9** | **Human Factors & Crew Management**  | Critical for safety; covers fatigue management, teamwork, and leadership in maritime settings.           | Superintendents, training officers.         | Fatigue risk management (FRM) tools, crew selection criteria, leadership case studies.              |
| **10** | **Maritime History & Culture**       | Engaging for students; connects past to modern challenges (e.g., **Black Friday**, **Titanic**, **Pirates**). | History buffs, cultural studies students.    | Timeline of maritime milestones, cultural impact of seafarers, heritage ships.                     |
| **11** | **Offshore & Remote Operations**     | Growing niche; covers deep-sea, polar, and offshore roles (e.g., **Polar Class**, **ROVs**).          | Offshore crew, polar expedition students.     | Safety protocols, certs like **Polar Class**, remote operation training.                           |
| **12** | **Maritime Economics & Trade Routes**| Helps students understand global shipping (e.g., **Baltic Exchange**, **Singapore Port**).                 | Economists, logistics students.              | Trade route analysis, container shipping stats, cost of shipping per tonne.                        |
| **13** | **Crew Welfare & Mental Health**     | Underrated but critical; covers seafarer mental health, isolation, and support networks.               | Crew welfare officers, HR in shipping.      | Resources (e.g., **IMO’s Seafarers’ Welfare**), case studies, online counseling services.           |
